DISPUTE CORRESPONDENCE - CONTRACTOR'S LETTERS

Letter No. RPB/2024/089
Date: 11.05.2024

To:
The Managing Director,
Rajasthan Medical Services Corporation Ltd. (RMSCL),
Swasthya Bhawan, Tilak Marg, Jaipur – 302 015

Subject: Urgent Request for Site Possession - Hospital Construction Project
Reference: Work Order No. RMSCL/2024-25/Works/4782 dated 05.05.2024

Dear Sir,

We refer to the Work Order issued on 05.05.2024 for construction of 300-Bed Hospital at Udaipur. As per Clause 5 of the CPWD GCC 2020, site possession was to be handed over within 15 days of Work Order, i.e., by 20.05.2024.

We have already mobilized the following resources at the site boundary in anticipation of timely possession:
- 150 skilled and unskilled workers
- 2 JCBs
- 4 Concrete Mixers
- 1 Tower Crane
- Complete scaffolding set
- Construction materials worth ₹45 Lakh

However, we observe that the existing structure on the site has not yet been demolished, and municipal NOC is still pending. We request RMSCL to expedite these prerequisites to avoid idle resource costs.

Awaiting your immediate response.

Yours faithfully,
For M/s. Rajputana Builders Pvt. Ltd.
Project Manager

***

Letter No. RPB/2024/095
Date: 15.05.2024

To:
The Managing Director,
RMSCL, Jaipur

Subject: Reminder: Site Possession Still Not Granted
Reference: Our Letter No. RPB/2024/089 dated 11.05.2024

Dear Sir,

We reiterate our request for immediate site possession. Our resources are now idle for 5 days, causing significant financial impact. Per Clause 10CC of GCC, any delay in site handover shall be considered an Employer's delay and shall be compensable.

Please arrange site possession by 18.05.2024 to avoid escalation.

Yours faithfully,
For M/s. Rajputana Builders Pvt. Ltd.
Director

***

Letter No. RPB/2024/102
Date: 18.05.2024

To:
The Managing Director,
RMSCL, Jaipur

Subject: Formal Notice of Delay and Claim for Idle Costs
Reference: Work Order No. RMSCL/2024-25/Works/4782

Dear Sir,

This is to formally record that site possession is still not granted as of today (18.05.2024), 13 days after the Work Order date. We hereby:

1. Record this delay as Employer's delay under CPWD GCC Clause 5.
2. Reserve our right to claim compensation for idle resources from 20.05.2024 onwards.
3. Request immediate intimation of the revised date of site possession.

Yours faithfully,
For M/s. Rajputana Builders Pvt. Ltd.
Director